## What a `type: concept-group` instance is

A first-class CROSS-CUTTING FACET MEMBERSHIP entity — analog of `iso-thes:ConceptGroup` from ISO 25964.  A concept-group is used for SUBSET GROUPING across the tag vocabulary, ORTHOGONAL to the broader/narrower hierarchy.  Whereas the hierarchy answers "what's narrower than X?", concept-groups answer "what subset shares some cross-cutting property?" — e.g., "deprecated tags", "high-traffic tags", "tags introduced in v0.7.x".

## When to materialize a concept-group

- A subset of tags shares a cross-cutting property worth naming explicitly (status / lineage / facet)
- The subset doesn't fit cleanly into a single hierarchical scheme
- The grouping needs to be queryable separately from hierarchy walks

